{"name":"Forbidden Blackberry","hex":"#323f75","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"forbidden","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Not allowed; specifically disallowed."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["past participle of forbid"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/forbidden"},{"term":"blackberry","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A fruit-bearing shrub of the aggregate species Rubus fruticosus and some hybrids.","The soft fruit borne by this shrub, formed of a black (when ripe) cluster of drupelets."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To gather or forage for blackberries."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/blackberry"}],"entries":[{"title":"Blackberry","blocks":[{"text":"A blackberry is an edible fruit produced by many species in the genus Rubus in the family Rosaceae, hybrids among these species within the subgenus Rubus, and hybrids between the subgenera Rubus and Idaeobatus. The taxonomy of blackberries has historically been confused because of hybridization and apomixis so that species have often been grouped together and called species aggregates."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/78/Ripe%2C_ripening%2C_and_green_blackberries.jpg/330px-Ripe%2C_ripening%2C_and_green_blackberries.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Blackberry"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/be/Rubus_fruticosus_Luc_Viatour.JPG/500px-Rubus_fruticosus_Luc_Viatour.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/be/Rubus_fruticosus_Luc_Viatour.JPG/1280px-Rubus_fruticosus_Luc_Viatour.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/be/Rubus_fruticosus_Luc_Viatour.JPG/500px-Rubus_fruticosus_Luc_Viatour.JPG?utm